## Compatibility change

- Added nine pinned Java heartbeat DTO cases for positive leading-dot integer
  tokens, String-field rejection, explicit-plus acceptance, and incomplete
  exponent conversions. The corpus now has 1,111 cases.
- Rust preserves leading-dot token provenance through typed DTO decoding so
  numeric fields can accept `.5` while String fields reject it. Explicit `+.5`
  and negative `-.5` keep their Java behavior. General `serde_json::Value`
  parsing continues to decode `.5` as a number.
- Incomplete `1e`, `1e+`, `1e-`, suffix forms, and trailing-dot exponent forms
  normalize to the observed numeric prefix and Java Float/Double String form.
- This closes these Fastjson token branches only. Broad P18-V01
  source/API/settings/input/error/control-flow and reverse-export
  reconciliation remains PARTIAL.

